# UIReqs frames that compare-uireqs-frames.sh passes to the frame-compare tool as --informational: compared
# and reported, but never failing the comparison. Everything not listed here is strict.
# One entry per line: a whole group (the folder directly under frames/<Orientation>/), or one feature of a
# group as <Group>/<feature file name without extension>. '#' starts a comment.

# Whole groups: frames depend on playback/loading timing, and the NUMBER of frames a run saves varies.
AudioPlayer
Lottie
MediaPlayer
VideoPlayer
WebView

# Single features, measured (2026-09-22, WP0.2): these differed between three runs of identical code
# (every strict UIReqs project run three times, all three pairs compared). Features identical across all
# three pairs stay strict.
# animation: the enabled/disabled visual-state transition is caught part-way
Buttons/ButtonCommand
# animation: the flyout's close transition is caught part-way
Buttons/DropDownButton
# animation: the checked/unchecked visual-state transition is caught part-way
Buttons/ToggleButton
# GL timing: the GL canvas content depends on when the GL frame lands
Graphics3DGL/Graphics3DGLInTheTree
# drag inertia: the swipe's settling position varies
Items/FlipView
# drag inertia: the scroll position after the drag varies
Items/ListView
# animation: the selection indicator's slide is caught part-way
Items/SelectorBar
# drag inertia: the scroll position after the drag varies
Navigation/ScrollViewer
# indeterminate progress: the indicator position depends on elapsed time
Range/ProgressBar
# animation: the fade's midway frame depends on elapsed time
ThemeFocus/Animation
# ANDROID-ONLY (measured 2026-09-23, AP2L2 stability s2): the wheel scenario shows the Fluent scroll
# indicator of the mouse-scrolled ScrollViewer, caught at a timing-dependent moment of its fade
AndroidNative/native_scrolling
